  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 1.4.0 - Toast & Snackbar Notifications:\n\nNEW FEATURES:\n• Toast Notifications: Lightweight, non-interactive notifications for quick status updates\n  - Configurable position (Top/Bottom) and duration (Short 2s, Long 3.5s, or custom)\n  - Optional icons using existing DialogType\n  - Configurable stacking behavior (Stack, Replace, Queue)\n• Snackbar Notifications: Actionable notifications with optional buttons\n  - Action button with callback support (UNDO, RETRY, VIEW, etc.)\n  - Short (4s), Long (7s), or Indefinite duration options\n  - Swipe-to-dismiss support\n  - Returns SnackbarResult (ActionClicked, Dismissed, TimedOut)\n• New Localization Strings: Added DISMISS, UNDO, RETRY translations for EN, ES, FR, DE\n\nIMPROVEMENTS:\n• Non-blocking notifications allow continued user interaction\n• Multiple notifications can stack vertically with configurable max count\n• Consistent theming with existing dialog components\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n• None - fully backward compatible with v1.3.0\n\nVersion 1.3.0 - Hierarchical Menus & Critical Bug Fix:\n\nNEW FEATURES:\n• Hierarchical Action List Support: ActionItem.SubItems property enables multi-level menu navigation\n• Seamless Navigation: Navigate through menu hierarchies within a single dialog instance\n• Automatic Back Navigation: Cancel/Back button automatically handles submenu navigation\n• Unlimited Nesting: Support for any depth of menu hierarchies\n\nBUG FIXES:\n• CRITICAL: Fixed \"duplicate key\" exception when showing dialogs immediately after ActionListDialog dismissal\n• Fixed race condition where PopAsync wasn't awaited before returning result\n• Ensures ActionListDialog is fully removed from Mopups stack before caller continues\n\nIMPROVEMENTS:\n• Better async handling in dialog dismissal for smoother transitions\n• Improved reliability when chaining multiple dialogs\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n• None - fully backward compatible with v1.2.0\n\nVersion 1.2.0 - Title & Description Customization:\n\nNEW FEATURES:\n• Title MaxLines Support: Configure maximum number of lines for dialog titles via DialogTheme.TitleMaxLines (default: 2)\n• Title LineBreakMode: Configure how titles are truncated/wrapped via DialogTheme.TitleLineBreakMode (default: TailTruncation)\n• HTML Description Support: Enable HTML formatting in descriptions via DialogTheme.DescriptionTextType (default: Text)\n• Theme-level Control: Apply formatting globally through theme settings for consistent UX\n\nKNOWN LIMITATIONS:\n• HeadTruncation and MiddleTruncation may not render correctly on Windows due to MAUI framework limitations\n• For cross-platform compatibility, use TailTruncation (default), WordWrap, CharacterWrap, or NoWrap\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n• None - fully backward compatible with v1.1.0\n\nVersion 1.1.0 - Enhanced Action List Dialog & Improved UX:\n\nNEW FEATURES:\n• Multi-line Description Support: ActionListDialog now supports 2, 3, or more lines for item descriptions\n• Configurable Line Break Modes: Choose between TailTruncation, WordWrap, CharacterWrap, HeadTruncation, and MiddleTruncation\n• Dynamic Description Updates: Change DescriptionMaxLines and DescriptionLineBreakMode properties after dialog creation\n• Intelligent Scrolling: Automatically shows scrollbar when content exceeds dialog height based on line settings\n\nIMPROVEMENTS:\n• Fixed Dialog Height: ActionListDialog now maintains consistent height with scrollable content area\n• Instant Dismissal: All dialogs now respect DialogTheme.EnableAnimation setting for instant or animated dismissal\n• Better UX: Controls are disabled immediately on interaction to prevent double-taps and accidental multiple selections\n• Optimized Layout: Switched to Grid-based layout for better text wrapping and performance\n\nBUG FIXES:\n• Fixed cancel button being cut off at bottom of ActionListDialog\n• Fixed scrollbar not appearing for multi-line descriptions\n• Fixed height calculation to account for variable description line counts\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n• None - fully backward compatible with v1.0.0\n\nPrevious release v1.0.0:\n• 7 dialog types: Alert, Confirm, Prompt, Editor, Loading, ActionList, ColorPicker\n• Built-in dark/light theme support with automatic detection\n• Internationalization support (English, Spanish, French, German)\n• Custom icon support with platform-specific optimizations\n• Cross-platform support (iOS, Android, Windows, macOS)",
